**Anonymization contract:** The capture snippet removes every `data-attrs`
attribute, every query string in `href`, `src`, `data-href`, and `action`, and
zeroes any run of 6 or more digits in a URL path. Fixtures are therefore not
byte-faithful. Do not write a test that asserts on a query parameter or a
numeric profile id. `spike/README.md`, "Risks found", holds the detail.
**Saved list behavior:** The list loads more entries on scroll (20 at the top of
the page, 85 at the bottom) and does not virtualize. A parser must scroll to the
bottom to see every entry, then can read the full list in one pass.
**Milestone 1 decisions (see the design doc):** direct Dexie access with
`useLiveQuery` and no messaging layer, with the Milestone 2 companion panel
deferred to an extension-origin iframe; WXT as the extension shell, which closes
the WXT-vs-CRXJS question; dense integer `sortOrder`; restore merges by URL
through `ingestCard()` rather than replacing; tests cover `domain/` and `db/`
with `fake-indexeddb` and skip the React layer.
