### 2026-08-31 - Milestone 4 implemented: board button, tags, library export

**What changed:** All six tasks of
`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-31-milestone-4.md` are written and committed
(`0f3d256`, `83e7d6b`, `97c18fd`, `a43852d`, `0785f8b`, and this one). The
manual checks are NOT run.

1. **Board button.** `PanelMessage` gains `{ type: 'open-board' }`; the reading
   panel footer has an "Open the board" button that sends it, and the
   background answers by calling the existing `openBoard()`. The panel does not
   open the tab itself, because `openBoard()` owns the `boardTabId` key and a
   second writer produces a duplicate tab.
2. **Tags.** New pure `domain/tags.ts` (`normalizeTag`, `addTag`, `removeTag`,
   `allTags`). `normalizeTag` strips `,` `[` `]` `"` before it trims, because
   `domain/markdown.ts` writes tags as a YAML flow sequence and any of those
   four breaks the whole frontmatter block. `CardFilter` gains `tags: string[]`
   and `visibleCards` requires a card to carry EVERY selected tag, the same
   narrowing direction as the query and the maximum. `ui/TagEditor.tsx` mounts
   in `CardEditor`'s body so both editors get it from one edit; it reads the
   vocabulary with its own `useLiveQuery(allCards)` rather than taking a prop.
   `Toolbar` renders a horizontally scrolling tag strip INSIDE the fixed-height
   toolbar row, hidden when the board has no tags. See "Corrections" 2 and 4 in
   the plan.
3. **Substack section removed.** `liked`, `commented`, and `unsavedFromSubstack`
   are gone from `Card`, `createCard`, the factory, and stored rows, the last
   by a Dexie `version(3)` upgrade whose store string is identical to v2. The
   detail panel loses its Substack heading and three checkboxes. A backup
   written before this milestone still restores; its cards land carrying three
   dead booleans that nothing reads. Accepted, per the design.
4. **Library export.** `STATUS_LABELS` moves to `domain/card.ts` so
   `domain/markdown.ts` can title the columns without importing from `ui/`
   (three older copies stay in `ui/Board.tsx`, `ui/ReadingPanel.tsx`,
   `ui/CardTile.tsx`; consolidating them is an open question). `toMarkdown`'s
   quote-and-notes body is factored into `cardBody(card, level)`, shared with
   the new `toLibraryMarkdown(cards, now)` at heading level four.
   `ui/downloadFile.ts` holds the blob-and-anchor sequence, now shared by
   `exportCard`, `BackupControls`, and the new `ui/ExportAllButton.tsx`.
   `ExportAllButton` takes `App`'s already-filtered `shown` array, so the
   export composes with every filter, and records nothing: a bulk snapshot is
   not a note for an article and must not touch `exportVersion`.

**Why:** Milestone 4 is release polish. Every item moves data across a boundary
the extension already sits on both sides of: no new permission, no tab opened,
no page read. The fifth named item, the self-filling Add-by-URL form, needs a
page nobody is looking at and became Milestone 5.

