### 2026-08-31 - Fix the board crash on a finished sync, and show the sync warning

**What changed:** Two bugs, found by tracing one report of the board's error
boundary firing after a Sync Saved run. First, `summarize` in
`src/ui/SyncButton.tsx` was still its `throw new Error('not implemented')` stub,
so every clean sync crashed the whole board. The developer wrote it: four
guarded `bits.push` calls and an `entriesSeen` fallback for the run that changed
nothing. Second, `applySync` writes `syncWarning` to the card and no component
read it, so an unsaved article produced no visible warning anywhere.
`CardTile` now renders it and `styles.css` gives it the same red as
`.notice.error`. Also removed a stale `TODO(human)` marker left on
`parseItemMeta` in `domain/saved.ts`, which has been implemented since `d525c9e`.

**Why:** The crash looked like a board or database fault and was neither. The
error boundary wraps the whole app and `SyncButton` mounts inside `Toolbar`, so
one throwing helper in a toolbar child unmounts every column. A reload cleared it
because `reply` resets to `null` and `summarize` is never reached. The cards were
never at risk: `applySync` had already committed before the render threw, which
is the layering doing its job.

The second bug is a hole in the plan rather than a defect in the code. The
Milestone 3 plan's file table gives `CardTile.tsx` only "show a non-read medium"
and never assigns the warning to any file, so `applySync` wrote a field with no
reader. The design's definition of done at line 62 requires it
("carries a visible warning") and `MANUAL-CHECKS.md` line 246 checks for it.
The card face was chosen over `DetailPanel` because triage happens on the board,
and a warning you must open a card to find misses the moment it matters.

The warning text stays in `db/sync.ts`, which owns the rule that decides when it
applies. `CardTile` only renders it. Rejected: joining it to `statusLabel`'s
bits, which would have muted a warning into the same grey metadata line as
"notes · 2 quotes".

**Files:** `extension/src/ui/SyncButton.tsx`, `extension/src/ui/CardTile.tsx`,
`extension/src/ui/styles.css`, `extension/src/domain/saved.ts`,
`docs/learning-notes.md`.

**Verification:** `npm run compile` clean. `npm test` 244 passed, 1 todo, 13
files. `npm run build` clean. All three dependency-rule greps OK. The two manual
checks that cover the warning (`MANUAL-CHECKS.md` lines 246 and 247) are NOT run
and stay unticked; nothing tests `src/ui/`.

**State after:** A finished sync reports its counts instead of crashing the
board, and a card whose article left the Saved list shows the warning in red on
its face. Seven of the eleven "Saved sync" checks passed on 2026-08-31, all of
them upstream of the warning. The six remaining are unticked.

**Next up:** Run the eleven "Saved sync (Milestone 3)" manual checks in
`extension/MANUAL-CHECKS.md`. Lines 246 to 248 are the ones this entry touches.

**Open questions:** Whether the warning also belongs in `DetailPanel` next to
the "Unsaved from Substack" checkbox. Those are different facts, per the design,
and showing them side by side may clarify or may confuse. Real use answers it.

