### 2026-08-30 - Write the Milestone 2B design, and cut the vault out of it

**What changed:** Wrote
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-30-milestone-2b-design.md`. No code changed.
2B is now three things, not four: Markdown serialization, the versioned
download, and the offer to move a card to Processed.
**Why:** The vault write was in the scope until the brainstorm reached its first
real question — whether a re-export into an Obsidian vault should overwrite the
note or sit beside it as a `(v2)`. Both answers are defensible and neither is
answerable from a document. The vault also drags in the File System Access API,
a persisted directory handle, a write permission that lapses between browser
sessions, and a settings surface, none of which is needed to get a note out of
the extension. It moves to its own spec, to be written once real exported notes
exist in a real vault and the overwrite question is a question about files the
developer can see.

The rest of the design, in short:

`domain/markdown.ts` holds `toMarkdown` and `exportFilename`, both pure and
importing types only, sibling to `domain/backup.ts`. `db/cards.ts` gains
`recordExport`. `ui/exportCard.ts` is the fifteen lines of glue and
`ui/ExportButton.tsx` is the one component both editors mount, because `src/ui/`
has no tests and writing the blob-and-anchor sequence twice would put two
untested copies of the same error handling in two files that drift.

`chrome.downloads` was rejected. It offers real filename control and costs a new
permission, a message round trip, and a collision: `conflictAction: 'uniquify'`
appends its own ` (1)` on top of this design's ` (v2)`.

**The export is recorded after the file is written, not before.** A counter
bumped ahead of a failed download leaves a version number for a file that does
not exist. In the chosen order the worst case is a duplicate file, which is
recoverable. Order the steps so the irreversible one runs first.

`exportVersion` counts exports, not files on disk. Delete a `(v2)` by hand and
the next export is still `(v3)`. The extension has no read access to Downloads
and asks for none, so the number is an honest history rather than a confident
wrong inventory.

`ReadingPanel`'s private `moveTo` moves into `db/cards.ts` as `moveCardTo`,
because the Processed offer needs the same move from two components and `src/ui/`
has no tests. That converts a manual check into an automated one.

**The three amendments to `implementation-plan.md`**, each recorded in the
spec's "Amendments to earlier documents" section: the vault write leaves
Milestone 2; the frontmatter grows from seven keys to eight, gaining
`reading_minutes`, because reading time is what the board triages on; and the
exported file labels a lost quote locator with an italic marker line, where the
reliability rule had described only the panel doing it.

