### 2026-08-30 - Capture selected text as quotes (2A Task 7, code only)

**What changed:** Task 7 Steps 1 to 13. New `domain/quote.ts` with `createQuote`
and `resolveQuote`, and `domain/quote.test.ts` with 11 tests.
`substack/extract.ts` gained `readSelection()`. `db/cards.ts` gained
`addQuote()`. `background.ts` gained a `runtime.onMessage` listener that answers
`capture-selection` by injecting `readSelection` into the panel's tab.
`ReadingPanel.tsx` gained a Capture quote button, a capture-error notice, and an
effect that re-checks every quote against the article text and writes
`locatorLost`.
**Why:** This is the task that closes the reading loop: select a sentence, press
a button, and the quote lands on the card with a comment box beside it. Three
decisions are worth keeping.

`resolveQuote` searches with a whitespace-tolerant regex built from the quote
and run over the ORIGINAL article text, rather than normalizing both sides and
calling `indexOf`. The function returns a character offset into the string it
was handed, and collapsing whitespace in the article shifts every offset past
the first collapsed run. Normalizing the needle instead keeps the haystack
addressable.

The four decisions the plan left open went: whitespace runs collapse and nothing
else does, so an author who changed case or punctuation made an edit and
`locatorLost` reports it; two matches the prefix cannot separate return null,
because "it is in two places" is not an answer to "where is it" and a confident
wrong offset is worse than a visible label; a match at a new offset is still the
same quote, so inserting a paragraph does not mark everything below it lost; and
a quote spanning a paragraph break still matches, which is the whitespace rule
doing its work.

