### 2026-08-30 - Stop trusting a stale canonical link (2A Task 6, Step 17 fix)

**What changed:** `domain/url.ts` gained `resolveArticleUrl(tabUrl,
canonicalUrl)`, and `background.ts` now calls it instead of taking
`meta.canonicalUrl ?? tabUrl`. The canonical link only wins when
`articleKey(canonical) === articleKey(tabUrl)`; otherwise the address bar wins.
**Why:** Step 17 check 3 failed. On `www.theworkthatholds.com` the card came
back with the right title and publication but the URL
`https://www.theworkthatholds.com/`. Substack is a React SPA and
`<link rel="canonical">` is server-rendered rather than react-helmet managed -
`og:title` carries `data-rh="true"`, the canonical does not. A client-side
navigation into an article swaps the helmet tags and leaves the previous page's
canonical in the head. Confirmed in the console (`location.href` on the article,
canonical and og:url on the home page) and by a hard reload producing a correct
card. The plan named a fourth fixture as the remedy for this check failing;
that was wrong and is not what landed. A fixture is a copy of the SERVER's HTML,
and the server's canonical is correct - I fetched both pages to confirm. The
fixture would pass and prove nothing. Slug-only comparison was the rejected
alternative: it would keep a fresh canonical that points at a publication's
other domain, which helps dedup, but it can also accept a stale canonical from a
different publication that happens to share a slug. Storing a URL from the wrong
publication is the expensive mistake, and Substack redirects a publication's
`*.substack.com` address to its custom domain, so the case slug-comparison would
have won is already rare.
**Files:** `extension/src/domain/url.ts`, `extension/src/domain/url.test.ts`,
`extension/src/entrypoints/background.ts`, `changes.log`.
**Verification:** `cd extension; npx vitest run` passes, 151 tests and 1 todo
across 8 files. `npx tsc --noEmit` reports nothing. `npx wxt build` is clean and
the injected-function check still prints `OK: self-contained` twice. Re-checked
by hand on the live custom-domain article: a card with the correct URL. NOTE:
running `npx vitest run` from the REPOSITORY root instead of `extension/` sweeps
`.worktrees/task-5-reading-panel/` and reports 76 failures that belong to that
stale worktree, not to this code.
**State after:** Step 17 checks 2 and 3 pass. Checks 1 and 4 through 7 have not
been run in this session.
**Next up:** Finish Step 17 checks 1 and 4 through 7, then Step 18, then commit
all of Task 6.
**Open questions:** The same staleness can hit `meta.title`, `meta.author`, and
`meta.publication` on a client-side navigation. `og:title` is helmet-managed and
did update, but JSON-LD carries no `data-rh` either, so `publication` may have
been read off the previous page and happened to match. Not investigated.

