### 2026-08-29 - Verify the schema version 2 migration by hand

**What changed:** Ran the "Migration to schema version 2" section of
`extension/MANUAL-CHECKS.md` against a real browser and ticked its three boxes.
Rewrote that section's setup steps, which were wrong the first time. Marked the
same-slug dedup check as covered by tests rather than run by hand.
**Why:** Nothing tests `src/ui/`, and the migration writes to a real reader's
board. The first attempt appeared to fail: adding the `open.substack.com` route
to a pre-fix card produced a second card. The cause was the recipe, not the
code. The setup said to delete the database only on a `VersionError`, but Dexie
does not throw when version 1 code opens a version 2 database. It opens it,
reports `verno` 1, and writes rows with no `articleKey`. The version on disk
stays at 2, so the version 2 build sees a current database and skips
`.upgrade()`. The board then held keyless rows, which are absent from the
`articleKey` index and invisible to the lookup in `ingestCard`. The setup now
